  "id": "COMPOUND:295 - PROTEIN:5412",
  "verbalization": "Mitomycin's relationship with SK-MEL3 is supported by multiple indirect pathways, all of which converge through the enzyme [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This enzyme is identified as a target of both palmarumycin CP18 and Lysine-specific demethylase 4C, which in turn are targets of mitomycin. The shared involvement of this enzyme in the target pathways of mitomycin suggests a potential mechanism by which mitomycin exerts its effect on SK-MEL3. The evidence is consistent across different paths, with varying scores indicating the strength of the relationships, but all pointing to a central role for this enzyme in mediating the interaction between mitomycin and SK-MEL3. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions, emphasizing the importance of the enzyme as a key mediator in the drug's action.",
